WEBVTT

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:34.070
My brother would only say it wasn't bad,

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.770
but I packed some in my lunch, 
so would you taste it later?

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.840
I can't wait!

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:46.380
I kind of want to use the Flight card 
to take a walk through the sky...

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.190
That sounds lovely.

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:50.370
You must let me film it, when you do.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.550
In your new costume, of course.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:55.990
Speaking of costumes...

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.060
This is true of yours, of course,

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:01.310
but Li-kun's is coming along nicely, too.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.320
You've grown taller.

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:08.220
Have I?

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.720
You look so much more manly!

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:11.930
Huh?

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.960
Er, but why are you measuring me?

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:19.360
I also wanted to see you wear 
a costume that I made.

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:24.830
I'll make them look beautiful, 
for both of you!

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:31.330
<b>Sakura, the Clock, and a 
Hide-and-Seek Game</b>

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.090
Once I've finished the tacking,

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:36.460
I'll need both of you to try them on.

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:38.460
You will, won't you?

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:39.800
S-Sure.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.560
<i>I'm kind of excited to see Syaoran-kun 
in his costume, though.</i>

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.670
Sakura-san! Tomoyo-san!

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.940
Akiho-chan...

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.380
Good morning!

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.820
Good morning.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:53.950
Morning!

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:55.140
Good morning.

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:57.370
Morning, Momo-chan!

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.940
"Good morning."

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.810
Same to your little friend, too!

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:08.280
Yeah! I brought Kero-chan!

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.530
Good morning, Kero-san.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.310
<i>Can't breathe... It's strangling me...</i>

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.720
<b>I saw a field 
of flowers...</b>

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.280
You walk to school, Akiho-chan?

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.220
Yes, since it's close.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.350
What's your house like?

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:31.910
It's a stand-alone house.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:37.210
I heard that a boy my age, who came here 
from England, lived in it before me.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:37.730
Huh?

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.510
Could that be...

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.120
Do you have a picture of the house?

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.020
Y-Yes.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.770
It's Eriol-kun's house!

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:58.160
So there was another overseas 
transfer student before me?

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:00.760
When we were in elementary school.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.630
His name was Eriol-kun.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.920
He was so mature and such a wonderful person.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.590
Where is he now?

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:08.310
He went back to England.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:11.170
But we send each other letters 
and e-mails, sometimes.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.670
<i>He still hasn't replied...</i>

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.440
Sakura-san?

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.170
Is something wrong?

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.070
Nah.

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:25.560
You've also been to England, haven't you?

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:26.330
Yes.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.760
What was it like?

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.550
There was a lot of fog.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:32.280
And it was very cold in the winter.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.320
But...

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:38.600
It's where I found something 
very important to me.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:42.330
So...

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:46.350
This was just the right time to 
tell you about where I live.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.100
I actually...

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:51.560
Gimme a break.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.400
Who knows what would've happened 
if I'd fallen from that height?

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.150
S-Sorry.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.520
Be a little more careful in how 
ya handle me from now on!

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:01.950
So, is it about what she said earlier?

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.310
Yeah.

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:05.370
Then, she lives in Hiiragizawa's house.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:06.170
Yeah.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:08.030
I was really surprised.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:12.920
Of course, she was surprised when I said 
my friend used to live there, too.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:17.190
Anyway, she asked if we could 
all come visit her this Sunday.

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.670
To her house?

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.000
Yeah.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.520
She's been to lots of different countries,

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:25.530
and she said she'd show us the 
books she's collected there.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:27.550
She can't read the languages,

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:30.310
but she said some of them have 
pretty drawings and photos.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:33.620
Sorry, I have something to do on Sunday.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.810
Oh, too bad...

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:39.350
Apologize to Shinomoto for me, okay?

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:40.230
Sure.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.990
A-Actually...

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:49.400
What about the Sunday... after that?

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:56.090
U-Um... I've been practicing 
making rolled omelets.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:59.210
And it's warmer now, 
so if the weather's nice,

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:03.450
could we... um, go out together?

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:07.670
Well, if you don't mind going with me.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:13.630
Only if you don't mind going with me!

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.270
Uh, there was a flower.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:22.320
Yeah...

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.570
Hey! I'm here, ya know!

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:26.710
This world ain't just for you two!

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:28.510
I'm gonna eat some rolled omelets, too!

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:29.690
Lots and lots of—

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:35.790
One, two! One, two! One, two! One, two!

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.640
One, two! One, two!

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:38.850
Now, turn!

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:41.200
Be mindful of each pose!

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:43.950
Kinomoto-san, move forward a bit more.

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:45.460
Yes, ma'am!

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:55.450
<i>That's Tomoyo-chan and Akiho-chan!</i>

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:01.330
Okay, be sure you practice the 
choreography at home, too.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:02.720
Good work today.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:04.720
Thank you!

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.430
Great job!

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:10.510
Hey, that pose right after the 
turn is pretty hard, huh?

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:11.230
Yeah.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:14.340
If you turn too late, the pose—

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:18.520
Tomoyo-chan and Akiho-chan 
are working hard, too.

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:21.510
Yeah, we'll have to do the same!

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:24.450
I'm home!

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:26.710
Huh?

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:30.860
Welcome home.

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:32.590
<b>Fujitaka   I'll be home around 7:00 PM today. 

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:32.580
You're early.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:35.340
One of my jobs was called off today.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:36.990
The cake place?

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:38.470
No, the movers.

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:40.230
Pork chops for dinner.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.650
Yay!

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:45.910
I'll go change. Need help?

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:47.970
They're almost done already.

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:48.980
Just do your homework.

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:50.490
Okay.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:51.500
Sakura...

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:55.630
What?

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:57.540
It's just...

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:03.120
Mind if I put konjac in the rice?

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.910
Don't you dare!

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:06.760
Ugh! You're such a jerk!

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:09.980
Still going on, huh?

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:16.150
That's my takoyaki...

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:21.140
You said you'd be there 
if anything happened,

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:22.390
and all you do is sleep.

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:31.430
I'm home.

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:33.820
Same goes for this Sunday,

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.760
but I'm so excited for next Sunday, too.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:48.750
This place again...

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:56.550
It really is a clock.

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:10.580
Who are you?

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:13.410
Why do you show up in my dreams?

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:17.200
No... Is this even a dream?

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:21.880
Is there something you want to say to me?

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:24.110
Or something you want me to do?

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:30.750
Please! Answer me!

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:39.300
Sakura!

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:41.130
You're awake...

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.140
It happened again?

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:47.720
Yeah. That dream again...

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:48.730
Are you hurt?

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.210
I'm okay.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:51.730
But...

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:54.590
Who is that?

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:07.000
It really is Eriol-kun's house...

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:08.920
It certainly is.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:13.830
It feels like it's been so long 
since we were here.

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:15.370
I'm a little nervous...

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:17.500
Why? You've been here before.

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:21.650
Yeah, but it's the first time I've 
seen it as Akiho-chan's house.

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:26.240
<i>Yes?</i>

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:28.820
U-Um, I'm Kinomoto!

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:30.160
I'm Daidouji.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:31.480
<i>I'll open it now.</i>

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:36.570
It opened automatically before, too.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:37.650
Oh, yeah.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:38.990
<i>Come on in.</i>

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.450
O-Okay!

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.800
You're movin' really funny!

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.880
Welcome!

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:56.310
Thank you for inviting us.

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:57.460
Thank you!

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:00.210
I'm so happy you came!

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:01.580
Hello.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:12.860
Thank you for paying us a visit today.

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:16.700
Oh, no... Thank you for having us!

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:22.690
I've made all kinds of trouble for 
Kaito-san since I was a child.

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:25.540
My name is Yuna D. Kaito.

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:29.640
I take care of various matters for Akiho-san.

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:33.510
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:40.420
You have never once troubled me, Akiho-san.

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:43.680
Please come inside.

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:45.760
We will, thank you.

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:04.700
It looks different from when 
Eriol-kun lived here.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:06.360
Yes, it does.

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:08.870
What was he like?

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:10.410
He was very mature.

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:13.570
He must have been very mature!

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:15.870
You mentioned that before, too.

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:18.310
Well, Eriol-kun was really—

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:23.460
He had a very calm and collected personality.

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:25.940
Yes?

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:28.890
Pardon me.

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:36.980
That smells nice...

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:42.540
I brewed the cherry-blossom-flavored 
tea we received as a gift.

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:44.360
Thank you for bringing it!

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:46.760
Tomoyo-chan and I picked it out.

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:57.120
You handle it so beautifully.

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:59.330
This is something I do every day.

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:02.240
Akiho-chan, you prefer tea?

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:04.180
I don't like coffee very much.

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:05.460
What about café au lait?

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:08.470
As long as it has lots of milk in it.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:11.100
Hey, just like you, Sakura.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:12.350
Kero-chan!

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:21.730
I see no need to force yourself to 
drink something you dislike.

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:23.730
Y-Yes.

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:26.110
Enjoy.

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:28.110
Thank you!

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.030
It's so good!

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:38.530
I've had this tea before,

00:13:38.530 --> 00:13:40.200
but this is particularly delicious.

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.290
Thank you.

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:43.700
Please enjoy this, as well.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:49.970
Let's eat!

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:59.610
N-N-Nothing... I didn't say anything!

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:01.910
What's the matter?

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:04.290
I made a weird noise...

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.110
But it was cute.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.590
I'm in middle school now.

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:12.230
It's kind of embarrassing, 
so I've been trying not to do it.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:14.430
It's very good!

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:17.500
Thank you.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.620
I want some, too!

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:33.460
Yum!

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.510
It really is good!

00:14:37.510 --> 00:14:39.520
What shop is it from?

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.390
Actually, I made it here.

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:43.360
Oh, you made it?

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:48.560
He always makes my snacks, 
meals, and lunches for me.

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:50.530
That's amazing!

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.710
Not at all.

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:55.350
It's my job.

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:03.660
Akiho-chan?

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:06.640
Then, please make yourselves at home.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:11.800
If you need anything, you may contact me 
by internal line or at my cell phone.

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:22.910
Thank you for everything!

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:28.610
Akiho-chan?

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:33.530
Um!

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:34.960
When we finish the cake,

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:37.370
there's someplace I want to show you!

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:45.450
Are these all yours, Akiho-chan?

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:47.440
Not exactly...

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:50.960
My family collected all of these.

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:54.220
Everyone in your family must love to read.

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:55.370
Yes.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:16:00.330
My whole family loves books, so we collect 
them from every country we go to.

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:02.970
This is just a small part of the collection.

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:08.200
Wow... All of these?

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:10.970
I love books, too.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:14.690
I came to Japan because there 
was a book I wanted.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:16.860
You came for a book?

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:19.200
Well, partly. Also...

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:25.800
What's the matter?

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:34.050
Um... Didn't you say there 
was a book you really liked?

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:34.680
Yes.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:37.370
I'd love to see it, if you wouldn't mind.

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:38.690
Of course!

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:41.180
It's in my room. I'll go and get it!

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:47.830
Is it...

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:49.630
Yeah, I think it's a card.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.490
Did something happen?

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:53.570
No, I just sensed it.

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:55.780
But I'm pretty sure...

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:27.240
Huh?

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:28.600
Oh!

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:30.920
There aren't any books here...

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:32.610
Only in this spot.

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:36.440
Volumes 1 through 9 are here.

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:40.700
Then there's a gap, before it 
picks up with volume 18.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:43.740
She's not in the middle 
of reading them, is she?

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:45.090
Huh?

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:48.960
It's not just the books! 
The shelf's gone, too!

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:50.340
Oh!

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:53.350
Are you all right?

00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:56.850
I don't know... But...

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.090
Huh?

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:04.270
I-I'm touching something...

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:08.190
It seems like... the books are here.

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:10.310
But I don't see anything.

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:12.460
This must be...

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:14.060
Tomoyo-chan!

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:17.770
This could be dangerous, 
so stand back a bit, okay?

00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:18.770
O-Of course.

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:25.380
<i>Key that hides the forces of dreams.</i>

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:29.550
<i>Show me your true form!</i>

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:33.290
<i>Release!</i>

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:55.140
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:18:55.140 --> 00:18:58.460
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:02.170
<i>Secure!</i>

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:24.880
It really was a card.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:26.890
"Lucid"...

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:30.890
<b>Lucid</b>

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:30.510
Lucid.

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:38.340
Looks like this card makes things 
invisible, Tomoyo-cha—

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.860
I'm a bit worried about blur and low quality,

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:45.670
but you must make sacrifices, sometimes.

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:49.390
Sakura-chan, do a pose with the card!

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:51.320
O-Okay...

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:55.340
I left my smartphone behind, 
so Kero-chan's there, too.

00:19:55.680 --> 00:19:57.160
That's right!

00:19:57.160 --> 00:20:00.190
I couldn't bring him along, 
for something important again.

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:01.840
Kero-chan will pout about it...

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:03.700
Sakura-san! Tomoyo-san!

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:08.010
Sorry for taking so long! This is the book!

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:11.550
Is something wrong?

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:12.830
N-Nah!

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:14.620
So that's the book?

00:20:14.620 --> 00:20:15.470
Yes.

00:20:15.970 --> 00:20:17.170
This is it!

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:19.480
Huh? It doesn't have a title.

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:22.850
It's not written on the cover,

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:26.250
but it's called <i>Alice in Clock Land</i>.

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:28.920
<i>Alice in Clock Land</i>?

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:31.290
Not "Wonderland"?

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.710
No, it's not by the author who wrote

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:36.500
<i>Alice in Wonderland</i> and 
<i>Through the Looking Glass</i>,

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.180
but it's very interesting.

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:42.250
The cover is so pretty, too! 
The clock design—

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:49.190
<i>I feel like I've seen this clock, 
somewhere, before...</i>

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:51.760
<i>Where was it?</i>

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:54.730
Sakura-san?

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:59.230
Sorry! I was just fascinated 
by how pretty it is.

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:01.660
So what's it about?

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:05.180
I... I can't read it.

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:06.850
What language is this?

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:08.470
I don't know.

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:13.820
But I've learned to read it, so I have 
an idea of what the story is about.

00:21:13.820 --> 00:21:15.720
You're amazing, Akiho-chan!

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:17.220
No, not at all.

00:21:17.220 --> 00:21:19.510
I'd love to hear what it's about!

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:21.220
Well, it's...

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:25.040
Excuse me!

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:28.870
Hello?

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:30.270
Okay.

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:34.650
Kaito-san is asking if we'd like 
something cold to drink...

00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:36.240
Is it okay?

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:37.490
Of course!

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:49.350
Why can't we go to Japan?!

00:21:49.730 --> 00:21:54.110
Remember what Eriol said? It's not time yet.

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:56.600
But Sakura-chan is having trouble!

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:58.770
Scary things might be happening to her!

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:00.640
And Yue and Toya-kun, too!

00:22:01.090 --> 00:22:04.050
I realize you want to see them, but still...

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:08.640
Of course I do. But aren't you 
worried about Cerberus, too?

00:22:09.280 --> 00:22:10.880
Well, I have various concerns.

00:22:10.880 --> 00:22:12.660
Oh, just be honest!

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:14.700
You're being <i>too</i> honest.

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:17.760
If we went, there might be something 
we could do for them!

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:19.240
There isn't.

00:22:20.330 --> 00:22:21.490
Eriol...

00:22:21.970 --> 00:22:25.490
Right now, all we can do is wait...

00:22:26.460 --> 00:22:28.520
for the time to come.

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:12.440
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:14.250
Pay attention, kids...

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:19.730
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:19.730
<b>K</b>

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:17.270
It's "Leave It to Kero-chan!" 
Today, we'll be seeing...

00:24:17.270 --> 00:24:19.990
They're back again! Another battle costume!

00:24:19.990 --> 00:24:22.970
This is from last time, when she captured 
the card at Tomoyo-chan's house.

00:24:22.970 --> 00:24:25.590
It features stars in several places.

00:24:25.590 --> 00:24:29.740
It's elegant how the upper arm is fitted, 
but the sleeve opens up at the end.

00:24:29.740 --> 00:24:31.960
The best part is that it matches mine.

00:24:30.190 --> 00:24:31.200
<b>This will be cut in editing</b>

00:24:31.200 --> 00:24:37.240
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:31.200 --> 00:24:37.240
<b>K</b>

00:24:31.960 --> 00:24:35.540
But who knew Akiho lived in the 
house Eriol used to live in?

00:24:35.540 --> 00:24:38.830
Sakura's world continues to get deeper 
and deeper. Don't miss what's next!

00:24:38.830 --> 00:24:39.990
Ta-ta...

00:24:39.990 --> 00:24:42.330
Dad gave me tickets,

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:43.000
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:42.330 --> 00:24:44.870
so I'm going to the aquarium 
with Syaoran-kun!

00:24:45.370 --> 00:24:48.790
Huh? Onii-chan, you're working here?

00:24:49.160 --> 00:24:52.030
Next time, "Sakura's Thrilling 
Aquarium Visit."

00:24:49.960 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura's Thrilling Aquarium Visit</b>

00:24:52.030 --> 00:24:55.010
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>End</b>
